__screenshots__
coverage
dist
build
*.log
.env
.env.*

# Agent fan-out worktrees are full checkouts of this repo, and
# .claude/settings.local.json is machine-local. Neither belongs in
# a build context -- Stage 7 ran ten of them at once.
.claude
# Agent worktrees live in `.worktrees/`. A `docker build` run on the host
# from the shared checkout would otherwise copy every worktree open at
# build time into the image.
.worktrees

# Documentation. Nothing at runtime reads a `.md`, but `COPY . .` was baking
# every one of them into the image — so a docs-only merge really did change the
# layer. Excluding them is what makes skipping the build on a docs-only change
# provably correct rather than merely cheap.
*.md
**/*.md
docs
